From cc6867fa3e64be00e4cf44b8fd3b3b5f6d3dafc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:30:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: native Dolby Vision on HDMI outputs without
 HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA

i915 offers the Dolby Vision tunnel (DVBRIDGE_DV_STANDARD_LAB) on HDMI
from display version 9 on (Skylake to Comet Lake, UHD 6xx graphics), but
attaches HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA to an HDMI connector only from display
version 10 on (intel_hdmi_add_properties() of Linux 7.2.11). The capture
of the output state for native output required that property on the
kernel backend, so on display version 9 native output was announced and
never started: kodi.log said "native output not started
stage=output-state-capture", and the Dolby Vision page of the player
information said only "failed". The same was reported against CroqueMr's
Dolby Vision fork (its issue 23).

On the kernel backend the property is now optional. Native output sets it
to 0; the kernel refuses the tunnel with HDR metadata in the connector
state (intel_dv_lab_validate(), amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_check_connector()), and
a connector without the property can have none, so there is nothing of it
to keep or put back. Every other property of the transport stays
required, and so does HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA on nvidia-drm. kodi.log says,
for each native output, that the connector has no such property.

When the capture fails, it now says why (the property that is not there,
the value an enum lacks, a blob that cannot be read, another plane on the
CRTC), in the log line of the rejection, and the Dolby Vision page shows a
reason of its own, "capture" (string 31930: "the driver lacks something
DV needs (see the log)"), in place of "failed".

Host test (capture_state_test.cpp, with stand-ins for the DRM objects and
libdrm): 70 checks, among them that a connector of display version 9 is
captured and that the transport and the restoration stage only the
properties that are there. Built against DVBridgeState.cpp from before
this change, the case of display version 9 fails.
